WEBVTT

00:00:00.301 --> 00:00:02.445
Here's a home loan of four hundred thousand

00:00:02.486 --> 00:00:04.751
dollars at five per cent a year, compounded

00:00:04.811 --> 00:00:05.192
monthly.

00:00:06.215 --> 00:00:08.763
Repaying two thousand one hundred and forty-seven dollars

00:00:08.824 --> 00:00:11.915
twenty-nine a month clears it in thirty years.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.167
That time is called the term.

00:00:14.713 --> 00:00:16.546
A mortgage calculator shows it straight away.

00:00:17.553 --> 00:00:20.179
Now suppose you pay two thousand five hundred

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.222
dollars a month instead.

00:00:21.785 --> 00:00:23.560
That's about three hundred and fifty dollars more.

00:00:24.429 --> 00:00:26.062
How much sooner is the loan gone?

00:00:26.809 --> 00:00:27.511
Less than a year,

00:00:28.216 --> 00:00:29.019
two to five years,

00:00:29.522 --> 00:00:30.586
or more than five years?

00:00:31.271 --> 00:00:31.735
Make a guess.

00:00:32.471 --> 00:00:33.284
Look at the first month.

00:00:33.809 --> 00:00:35.953
The interest is charged on the four hundred

00:00:35.994 --> 00:00:38.460
thousand you owe, so it's one thousand six

00:00:38.501 --> 00:00:41.728
hundred and sixty-six dollars sixty-seven either way, rounded

00:00:41.769 --> 00:00:42.149
to the cent.

00:00:43.072 --> 00:00:45.301
Paying more can't change this month's interest.

00:00:45.884 --> 00:00:48.160
So every extra dollar goes straight to the

00:00:48.202 --> 00:00:48.443
debt.

00:00:49.488 --> 00:00:51.958
At the thirty-year repayment, the debt falls by

00:00:52.059 --> 00:00:53.986
four hundred and eighty dollars sixty-two.

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:56.895
At two thousand five hundred, it falls by

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:59.443
eight hundred and thirty-three dollars thirty-three,

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:01.089
nearly twice as much.

00:01:01.953 --> 00:01:02.885
And it doesn't stop there.

00:01:03.473 --> 00:01:05.676
The lower balance means less interest next month,

00:01:06.178 --> 00:01:07.259
and every month after,

00:01:07.781 --> 00:01:10.145
so even more of each repayment goes to

00:01:10.166 --> 00:01:10.505
the debt.

00:01:11.129 --> 00:01:13.019
To see the whole loan, let a digital

00:01:13.061 --> 00:01:13.885
tool do the months.

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:17.196
A mortgage calculator, or a spreadsheet, runs the

00:01:17.257 --> 00:01:18.881
recurrence row after row:

00:01:19.443 --> 00:01:22.170
multiply by one plus r, then subtract the

00:01:22.191 --> 00:01:22.591
repayment.

00:01:23.394 --> 00:01:25.417
Slide the repayment up to two thousand five

00:01:25.478 --> 00:01:27.761
hundred, and the balance reaches zero at the

00:01:27.843 --> 00:01:29.625
two hundred and sixty-fifth repayment.

00:01:30.328 --> 00:01:32.137
That last one only needs five hundred and

00:01:32.178 --> 00:01:33.484
forty dollars fifty-seven.

00:01:34.269 --> 00:01:37.181
That's twenty-two years and one month, so the

00:01:37.222 --> 00:01:39.149
loan is gone about eight years sooner.

00:01:39.894 --> 00:01:41.664
So the answer to the guess is more

00:01:41.685 --> 00:01:42.449
than five years.

00:01:43.194 --> 00:01:45.598
That last repayment is smaller because, by then,

00:01:45.619 --> 00:01:48.003
what's owed plus its interest is less than

00:01:48.024 --> 00:01:48.745
a full repayment.

00:01:49.522 --> 00:01:51.513
Here's a graph made the same way, for

00:01:51.594 --> 00:01:52.680
four different repayments.

00:01:53.383 --> 00:01:55.711
Each curve ends where its balance reaches zero,

00:01:56.094 --> 00:01:58.141
so you can read each term off the

00:01:58.182 --> 00:01:58.804
time axis.

00:01:59.587 --> 00:02:00.229
Thirty years,

00:02:00.733 --> 00:02:04.109
about twenty-two, about sixteen, and about thirteen.

00:02:05.095 --> 00:02:07.387
Each step up is another five hundred dollars

00:02:07.407 --> 00:02:07.649
a month.

00:02:08.353 --> 00:02:10.742
But the first five hundred saves almost six

00:02:10.803 --> 00:02:13.313
years, and the next saves only about three.

00:02:14.378 --> 00:02:16.668
On these curves, each extra five hundred dollars

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:18.778
buys less time than the one before.

00:02:19.469 --> 00:02:20.775
Why do the savings shrink?

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:23.844
Only the part of a repayment above the

00:02:23.945 --> 00:02:25.408
interest pays the debt down.

00:02:26.252 --> 00:02:28.198
The first month's interest here is about one

00:02:28.219 --> 00:02:30.989
thousand six hundred and sixty-six dollars sixty-seven.

00:02:31.733 --> 00:02:34.219
Pay exactly that interest, and the balance stays

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:35.643
at four hundred thousand for ever.

00:02:36.246 --> 00:02:38.093
That's called an interest-only repayment.

00:02:39.118 --> 00:02:41.005
Pay any less, and the balance grows.

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:44.057
Now plot the term against the repayment.

00:02:44.759 --> 00:02:47.783
Just above the interest-only line, a small extra

00:02:47.844 --> 00:02:49.305
amount makes a huge difference,

00:02:49.827 --> 00:02:52.590
from about seventy-nine years at seventeen hundred dollars

00:02:52.951 --> 00:02:54.813
to about thirty-six at two thousand.

00:02:55.616 --> 00:02:58.221
Far above it, the curve flattens, and extra

00:02:58.262 --> 00:02:59.785
money buys only a little time.

00:03:00.535 --> 00:03:02.959
Now keep the repayment at two thousand five

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.064
hundred and change the interest rate.

00:03:05.807 --> 00:03:07.833
Each rate is a separate loan, fixed from

00:03:07.874 --> 00:03:08.475
the first month.

00:03:09.279 --> 00:03:11.626
At five per cent, it takes about twenty-two

00:03:11.707 --> 00:03:12.027
years.

00:03:12.791 --> 00:03:14.598
At four per cent, about nineteen.

00:03:15.382 --> 00:03:17.389
At six per cent, about twenty-seven,

00:03:17.892 --> 00:03:20.362
and at seven per cent, nearly thirty-nine.

00:03:21.085 --> 00:03:23.488
So a rate rise of one point adds

00:03:23.529 --> 00:03:25.933
about five years, but a fall of one

00:03:25.974 --> 00:03:27.676
point saves only about three.

00:03:28.681 --> 00:03:29.124
Here's why.

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:33.135
A higher rate raises the interest-only line, so

00:03:33.256 --> 00:03:35.219
less of the same repayment is left for

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:35.680
the debt.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:37.906
And the closer that line gets to your

00:03:37.947 --> 00:03:40.091
repayment, the faster the term grows.

00:03:40.854 --> 00:03:43.441
This matters most for someone paying the thirty-year

00:03:43.483 --> 00:03:44.003
repayment.

00:03:44.626 --> 00:03:46.266
With a rate fixed at six per cent

00:03:46.307 --> 00:03:48.748
from the start, paying two thousand one hundred

00:03:48.769 --> 00:03:51.790
and forty-seven dollars twenty-nine stretches the term to

00:03:51.971 --> 00:03:53.331
almost forty-five years.

00:03:54.213 --> 00:03:55.455
At six and a half per cent, the

00:03:55.496 --> 00:03:57.860
first month's interest is two thousand one hundred

00:03:57.881 --> 00:03:59.745
and sixty-six dollars sixty-seven.

00:04:00.327 --> 00:04:03.073
That's more than the repayment, so the balance

00:04:03.134 --> 00:04:05.319
grows, and the loan is never repaid.

00:04:06.182 --> 00:04:08.347
A loan only shrinks when the repayment is

00:04:08.488 --> 00:04:10.052
more than the interest on the balance.

00:04:10.842 --> 00:04:12.150
Here's the idea in one line.

00:04:12.833 --> 00:04:15.263
Only what's left after the interest pays the

00:04:15.284 --> 00:04:15.846
loan down.

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:18.079
A bigger repayment leaves more.

00:04:18.804 --> 00:04:20.352
A higher rate leaves less.

00:04:21.055 --> 00:04:23.359
And if nothing's left, the loan never shrinks.

00:04:26.214 --> 00:04:26.662
Your turn.

00:04:27.228 --> 00:04:29.490
A loan of two hundred thousand dollars has

00:04:29.612 --> 00:04:32.274
interest at six per cent a year, compounded

00:04:32.335 --> 00:04:32.695
monthly.

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:35.658
The borrower repays one thousand dollars a month.

00:04:36.445 --> 00:04:38.880
Explain why the loan is never repaid.

00:04:39.688 --> 00:04:40.661
Pause here to answer.

00:04:51.307 --> 00:04:53.390
The monthly rate is half a per cent,

00:04:53.812 --> 00:04:55.995
so the first month's interest is half a

00:04:56.037 --> 00:04:58.480
per cent of two hundred thousand, which is

00:04:58.762 --> 00:04:59.522
one thousand dollars.

00:04:59.965 --> 00:05:01.242
That's the whole repayment.

00:05:01.727 --> 00:05:03.770
None of it reduces the debt, so the

00:05:03.831 --> 00:05:06.055
balance is still two hundred thousand next month,

00:05:06.618 --> 00:05:08.321
and the same thing happens every month.

00:05:08.925 --> 00:05:10.030
Two hundred months is wrong.

00:05:10.474 --> 00:05:12.943
Dividing the loan by the repayment ignores the

00:05:12.984 --> 00:05:13.304
interest.

00:05:15.072 --> 00:05:15.518
Last one.

00:05:16.228 --> 00:05:18.252
The graph shows the time taken to repay

00:05:18.273 --> 00:05:21.078
a four hundred thousand dollar loan at five

00:05:21.119 --> 00:05:24.004
per cent a year, compounded monthly, for different

00:05:24.105 --> 00:05:25.006
monthly repayments.

00:05:25.869 --> 00:05:28.035
Use the graph to estimate the monthly repayment

00:05:28.096 --> 00:05:30.663
needed to repay the loan in fifteen years.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:32.382
Pause here to answer.

00:05:43.147 --> 00:05:45.729
Find fifteen years on the term axis, go

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:47.791
across to the curve, then down to the

00:05:47.852 --> 00:05:48.632
repayment axis.

00:05:49.174 --> 00:05:51.461
It's about three thousand one hundred and sixty

00:05:51.502 --> 00:05:52.023
dollars a month.

00:05:52.887 --> 00:05:55.734
Doubling the thirty-year repayment, to about four thousand

00:05:55.776 --> 00:05:57.099
three hundred, is wrong.

00:05:57.781 --> 00:06:00.063
Halving the term doesn't double the repayment, because

00:06:00.364 --> 00:06:02.526
the shorter loan pays much less interest.

00:06:04.188 --> 00:06:06.691
So paying more shortens a loan, and a

00:06:06.752 --> 00:06:08.173
higher rate lengthens it,

00:06:08.675 --> 00:06:11.519
but never evenly, because only the part above

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:13.202
the interest pays the debt down.

00:06:14.104 --> 00:06:16.574
Calculators and graphs find terms for you.

00:06:16.997 --> 00:06:19.345
But how do you find one exactly, by

00:06:19.386 --> 00:06:19.707
hand?

00:06:20.869 --> 00:06:23.069
Here's a used motorbike, bought with a loan

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:25.431
of twenty thousand dollars at seven point two

00:06:25.472 --> 00:06:27.473
per cent a year, compounded monthly.

00:06:28.156 --> 00:06:30.093
The repayments are four hundred dollars a month.

00:06:30.839 --> 00:06:31.582
How many will it take?

00:06:34.501 --> 00:06:35.304
Here are the key notes.

00:06:35.947 --> 00:06:37.675
Pause the video if you need more time

00:06:37.736 --> 00:06:38.218
to copy them.
